---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="The Tier Guide — HUE Co." description="Three metals. Three price points. Stainless Steel PVD, 14k Gold-Filled, and 14k Solid Gold — which permanent jewelry tier is right for you?">

<!-- ── Hero ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="section--dark article-hero">
  <div class="container container--narrow">
    <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--light">Metal Guide</span>
    <h1 class="section-title section-title--xl article-hero__title">The Tier Guide</h1>
    <p class="section-subtitle">Three metals. Three price points. One perfect choice for you.</p>
    <div class="article-hero__meta">
      <span class="article-meta__cat">Metals</span>
      <span class="article-meta__sep">&middot;</span>
      <span class="article-meta__read">8 min read</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── Article Body ───────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="section section--cream">
  <div class="container container--narrow">
    <article class="article-body">

      <p class="article-lead">The most common question we get at HUE Co. isn't "does it hurt?" It's "which metal should I choose?" This guide is the honest answer — no upselling, no pressure, just the facts about each tier and who each one is right for.</p>

      <h2 class="article-h2">Tier 1 — Stainless Steel PVD &middot; From $42</h2>

      <h3 class="article-h3">What It Is</h3>
      <p>Stainless steel coated via Physical Vapor Deposition — a process that bonds a thin, extremely durable layer of gold-toned finish to the steel. The result is a chain that looks warm and refined while offering the durability of steel.</p>

      <h3 class="article-h3">Why It's Great</h3>
      <p>PVD coating is the most wear-resistant finish available for steel jewelry. It won't flake, chip, or peel under normal conditions. It's immune to sweat, chlorine, salt water, and UV exposure. You can wear it at the gym, in the ocean, and in the shower with zero degradation.</p>

      <h3 class="article-h3">Who It's For</h3>
      <ul class="article-list">
        <li>First-time permanent jewelry clients testing the lifestyle</li>
        <li>Athletes, surfers, swimmers, and anyone with an active daily routine</li>
        <li>Clients who want permanent jewelry without the gold price point</li>
        <li>Younger clients building their first stack</li>
      </ul>

      <h3 class="article-h3">Care Notes</h3>
      <p>Tier 1 requires the least maintenance of any option. Rinse with fresh water after chlorine or salt water exposure. Pat dry. Avoid direct, prolonged contact with harsh chemicals. That's genuinely all.</p>

      <div class="tier-callout tier-callout--t1">
        <div class="tier-callout__tier">T1</div>
        <div>
          <p class="tier-callout__headline">Stainless Steel PVD</p>
          <p class="tier-callout__price">$1.75/in + $30 weld — From $42</p>
          <p class="tier-callout__note">Charms from $12</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2 class="article-h2">Tier 2 — 14k Gold-Filled &amp; Argentium Silver &middot; From $72</h2>

      <h3 class="article-h3">What Gold-Filled Means</h3>
      <p>Gold-filled is a legally regulated term in the United States. To be called "gold-filled," a piece must contain at least 5% of its total weight in gold. That gold is mechanically bonded to a base metal — unlike plating, which is a thin deposit that can wear away. Gold-filled jewelry can last decades of daily wear without losing its finish.</p>

      <h3 class="article-h3">What Argentium Silver Is</h3>
      <p>Argentium is a modern silver alloy containing 93.5% pure silver (compared to sterling's 92.5%), with germanium replacing some of the copper in the alloy. The result: significantly better tarnish resistance than sterling silver, a brighter white finish, and better weldability. If you want a silver-toned permanent jewelry piece, Argentium is the right choice.</p>

      <h3 class="article-h3">Who It's For</h3>
      <ul class="article-list">
        <li>Clients who want the look and feel of gold without the solid gold price</li>
        <li>Anyone with sensitive skin who has reacted to lower-quality metals</li>
        <li>Clients who want something more elevated than Tier 1 for daily wear</li>
        <li>Clients building a multi-chain stack at a manageable price</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="tier-callout tier-callout--t2">
        <div class="tier-callout__tier">T2</div>
        <div>
          <p class="tier-callout__headline">14k Gold-Filled &amp; Argentium Silver</p>
          <p class="tier-callout__price">$3.75/in + $45 weld — From $72</p>
          <p class="tier-callout__note">Charms from $28</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2 class="article-h2">Tier 3 — 14k Solid Gold &middot; From $145</h2>

      <h3 class="article-h3">The Metal</h3>
      <p>14 karat gold is 58.5% pure gold, alloyed with other metals (silver, copper, zinc) for the durability required in wearable jewelry. Pure 24k gold is too soft to be worn daily — 14k is the sweet spot between gold purity and real-world wearability. It's the industry standard for fine jewelry.</p>

      <h3 class="article-h3">Yellow vs. White Gold</h3>
      <p>Both are available at HUE Co. Yellow gold has the classic, warm tone you associate with fine jewelry. White gold is alloyed with white metals (palladium, silver) and rhodium-plated for its cool, silver-like finish. Both are the same karat; the difference is entirely aesthetic.</p>

      <h3 class="article-h3">The Value Proposition</h3>
      <p>Solid gold has real melt value. If you ever wanted to repurpose the metal — unlikely, given that it's permanently welded to your wrist — it has actual market value. It's also the piece most likely to become an heirloom. Clients who choose Tier 3 often describe it as "the piece I'll still be wearing in twenty years." They're right.</p>

      <h3 class="article-h3">Who It's For</h3>
      <ul class="article-list">
        <li>Clients making an investment purchase — the "one piece, forever" mindset</li>
        <li>Anyone who wants the real thing, full stop</li>
        <li>Clients who care about resale or melt value</li>
        <li>The person who wants to pass something down</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="tier-callout tier-callout--t3">
        <div class="tier-callout__tier">T3</div>
        <div>
          <p class="tier-callout__headline">14k Solid Gold</p>
          <p class="tier-callout__price">$10.00/in + $75 weld — From $145</p>
          <p class="tier-callout__note">Charms from $75</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2 class="article-h2">Side by Side</h2>
      <p>Every tier is waterproof. Every tier is welded to your exact body. The differences are in the metal and what it means to you.</p>

    </article>

    <!-- Comparison Table -->
    <div class="table-wrap article-table-wrap">
      <table class="compare-table">
